{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","packSha":"fac868acb4f481e6f1f089e37ff82e1c4c610b1fb20efcca5ca569895ac7ae6f","packTokens":5856,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":67,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":678,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":939,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":4101,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":8,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Replace phone/email-based parts ordering with a self-service ordering portal\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Allow customers to quickly find parts using part numbers, product names, categories, and vehicle information\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Show each customer their applicable pricing and current stock availability\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Reduce manual order-entry work for office staff\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Give customers visibility into order status and invoices\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide staff with operational order queues and delivery information\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide management with basic sales and product reporting\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Maintain an auditable history of orders, invoices, customer accounts, and catalogue changes\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer authentication with sign-in, password reset, and account management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Build product catalogue with search, filtering, categories, and vehicle compatibility\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement customer-specific pricing and price list management\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Manage stock availability with ERP CSV imports\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-13\",\n  \"text\": \"Build basket and checkout workflow with delivery date rules\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-14\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement order management with status tracking and staff editing capabilities\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-15\",\n  \"text\": \"Build customer order history, cancellation, and repeat order functionality\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-16\",\n  \"text\": \"Implement invoice creation, viewing, PDF download, and payment tracking\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-17\",\n  \"text\": \"Build administrative tools for product, user, category, and price list management\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"Is the Customer Account Manager role in the first release? And can a Buyer see all of their company's orders (section 3.1) or only the orders they placed (section 3.2 implies only managers see other users' orders)?\",\n  \"answer\": \"No Account Manager role; every Buyer sees all of their company's orders and invoices\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"Which invoices can a customer see? Invoices are only created when an order becomes Delivered (section 29), so should the invoice list simply show every invoice that exists for the customer's company?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Customers see every invoice that exists for their company; invoices only exist once the order is Delivered\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"After confirmation, which status changes can staff make? In particular, can staff cancel a Confirmed or later order for a customer who phones in?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Staff move orders forward one step at a time and can cancel any order that is not yet Delivered\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What is recorded in the audit history for customer accounts and catalogue changes, and who can view it?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Who, when, and which fields changed (old and new values); admins only\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"Can customers create or edit their own delivery addresses, or are addresses maintained only by staff or admins?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Customers can only select from addresses that staff or admins maintain\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Customer Buyers can see all of their company's orders. Should saved basket templates also be shared with every Buyer in the company, or stay private to the Buyer who made them?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Templates are private to the Buyer who created them\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"There is no management role. Who can see the sales and product reports, and which reports are in the first release?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Office staff and admins; sales by period, sales by customer, and top products\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"How is stock checked when an order is placed or confirmed? Stock only changes with the nightly ERP import, and the portal never decrements it.\",\n  \"answer\": \"Compare the ordered quantity with the last imported quantity, without subtracting orders placed since the import\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a user sign in with an email and password matching an active account, starting an authenticated session that carries the user's role and, for a Customer Buyer, their customer company.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a signed-in user sign out, invalidating that user's session.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must lock an account for 15 minutes after 5 consecutive failed sign-in attempts, rejecting all sign-ins during that time with a message that the account is temporarily locked.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a user request a password reset, emailing a single-use reset link valid for 1 hour that lets them set a new password.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let an administrator invite a Customer Buyer or Office Staff user by email with a 7-day link to set a password and activate the account.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject sign-in and order submission for deactivated users or users of inactive companies while preserving their existing orders, invoices and history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators list users, deactivate/reactivate them, change roles among Customer Buyer, Office Staff and Administrator, or change a Buyer's company, showing role, company and status, keeping each Buyer linked to one company, applying changes on the user's next request, and keeping history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must restrict each Customer Buyer to only their own company's orders, invoices, prices, delivery addresses and account details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must restrict staff functions to Office Staff and Administrators and admin functions to Administrators, refusing unauthorized requests without making changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer search the catalogue by text term, matching product name, distributor code, manufacturer part number or brand, case-insensitively, returning only active products.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer filter the catalogue by a flat category, combinable with text or vehicle search.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer search by vehicle attributes (make, model, year, engine, fuel type, variant) returning active products with matching compatibility records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must show catalogue list and detail views with image, name, code, manufacturer, unit of sale, pack size, customer price and stock status, plus description and compatibility list on detail.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must display prices excluding tax from the price list assigned to the Buyer's company, in the configured currency.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must show 'Price on request' and block basket addition for products missing a price or whose price list is deactivated.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must derive stock status (Out of stock, Low stock, In stock) from last imported quantity and the configured low-stock threshold.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must run a scheduled stock import job that updates product quantities from a valid ERP CSV, skipping unknown codes and logging results.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must keep prior stock quantities unchanged and log a failed import with reason when the ERP file is missing, unreadable, or invalid, visible to Office Staff and Administrators.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must maintain one persistent basket per Buyer until submitted as an order or emptied.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must validate basket line quantity changes as whole numbers ≥1 and compute line totals and subtotal accordingly.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must calculate the earliest delivery date based on cutoff time, timezone and working days excluding weekends and listed non-working dates.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject order submissions with invalid delivery dates (non-working day, before earliest date, or beyond booking horizon), naming the broken rule.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer select only active delivery addresses maintained by staff for their company at checkout.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject order submissions where line quantities exceed last imported stock, returning the available quantity without altering stock or accounting for since-import orders.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 25,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must reject order submissions where reviewed prices differ from current prices or when a product has become 'Price on request', returning current prices for review.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 26,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must create an order with sequential number, Received status, order-time prices, delivery details and note upon passing validation, and empty the basket.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 27,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must keep existing order and invoice prices unchanged when price list prices are later changed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 28,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must allow Office Staff to change order status only to the next status in a defined sequence or to cancellation.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 29,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must record a timeline entry with new status, timestamp and acting user/system whenever an order's status changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 30,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff confirm a Received order only if stock and company status checks pass, recording the confirming user and time, or reject with the reason.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 31,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must email the order recipient a confirmation with order details and any staff-made changes when an order becomes Confirmed.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 32,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff cancel or reject a non-Delivered order with a required reason, recording it and emailing the recipient.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 33,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff amend a Received order's lines, dates, address and note, applying checkout rules and recording changes in an amendment history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 34,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must email the order recipient when staff change or remove order lines on a Received order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 35,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must email the order recipient when an order's status changes to Out for delivery.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 36,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff submit orders on behalf of active customer companies, applying the same validation rules as self-service checkout and recording the staff user as creator.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 37,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff view and filter the full order queue by customer, date range and status with specified fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 38,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff export a CSV delivery list for a given date containing all non-cancelled orders due that date with specified fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 39,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must show Office Staff and Administrators a dashboard with order status counts, due-today orders, invoice statuses and latest stock import result.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 40,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer list their company's orders, newest first, filterable by status and date range, with specified fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 41,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer view full order details including timeline, lines, totals, note and amendments.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 42,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer cancel their own company's orders only while Received, else reject with a message to contact the distributor office.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 43,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer repeat a previous order, adding available lines to the basket at current prices and flagging unavailable ones, without creating a new order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 44,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Buyer save and reuse named basket templates privately, using current prices and flagging unavailable products.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 45,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must create an Unpaid invoice with sequential number and specified fields when an order becomes Delivered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 46,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must compute invoice status (Paid, Overdue, Unpaid) based on payment and overdue-days setting.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 47,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let users list invoices according to their role scope, with specified summary fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 48,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let authorized users download an invoice PDF containing specified details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 49,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff mark an invoice as paid with a payment date, recording the user.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 50,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators manage product records (add, edit, retire) with specified fields, keeping retired products out of the catalogue but visible on existing orders/invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 51,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators manage single-level categories and product category assignments, applying changes to catalogue filtering.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 52,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators upload product images restricted to JPEG, PNG or WebP under 5 MB, replacing the previous image.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 53,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators manage vehicle compatibility records per product, applying changes to search and detail views.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 54,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators manage price lists and prices, and assign them to companies, applying changes to displayed prices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 55,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators create and edit customer companies with specified fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 56,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff edit limited company fields (contact, phone, billing address) but not price list or active status, which require admin rights.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 57,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff and administrators manage a company's delivery addresses with specified fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 58,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff search customers by name or account number and view their details, price list, status, users, orders and invoices.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 59,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let administrators edit and validate system settings (cutoff time, timezone, thresholds, dates, tax rate, currency) applied to subsequent calculations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 60,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must record an audit entry for every creation, change or deletion of key entities, capturing user, timestamp, entity and field changes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 61,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must restrict audit history visibility to administrators, filterable by type, record and date range, with no edit or delete capability.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 62,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let Office Staff and administrators request sales-by-period, sales-by-customer and top-products reports with on-screen and CSV output computed from invoice data.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 63,\n  \"text\": \"The portal must let a Customer Buyer submit an order directly through self-service checkout so it enters the Office Staff queue without requiring staff order entry.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}